---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About · Josh Approved"
  description="Why Josh Approved exists and how it works."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Nav variant="full" />

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lede">Josh Approved is a side project.</p>

      <p>
        After years building consumer apps in the tech industry, I wanted to do utility
        apps differently. The pattern I kept seeing: a simple tool wrapped in an account,
        an analytics SDK, and a paywall in front of the one feature people opened the app
        for. None of that is necessary to make a good timer or a good converter. So this
        exists.
      </p>

      <p>
        A Josh Approved app does one thing well, runs on your device by default, and
        stays out of your way. We charge only when we're covering a real cost — a server,
        an API. We use accounts only when the feature genuinely needs one, like
        cross-device sync.
      </p>

      <p>What you won't see: ads, hidden tracking, or nag screens.</p>

      <p>If we drift from this, the apps lose the badge.</p>
    </article>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 32px;
  }
  .prose {
    padding: 64px 0 32px;
  }
  .prose h1 {
    font-size: 48px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .container { padding: 0 20px; }
    .prose h1 { font-size: 36px; }
    .prose { padding: 40px 0 24px; }
  }
</style>
